<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Fyodor the Black</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1240–1299</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Fyodor Rostislavich</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Fyodor the Black, Fyodor Rostislavich, was a Rurikid prince of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/smolensk">Smolensk</a> who became prince of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yaroslavl">Yaroslavl</a> by marriage in the 1260s. He spent long periods at the court of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/golden-horde">Golden Horde</a>, married a khan's daughter and used Mongol support in Russian princely conflicts. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russian-orthodox-church">Russian Orthodox Church</a> later venerated him as a saint.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/fyodor-the-black.jpg" alt="Fyodor the Black" width="320" height="463" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Fyodorstratelate.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
